WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.148 --> 00:00:02.859
(marker squealing on white board)

00:00:02.859 --> 00:00:04.270
(jazzy music)

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.920
- One time, when I was in College,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.246
I went to knock on the
bathroom, it was last call,

00:00:08.246 --> 00:00:09.570
everyone was gone, but I knew

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.350
that there were two people
inside who left their tab.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.715
And I had of an idea where they were.

00:00:12.715 --> 00:00:13.548
(laughs)

00:00:13.548 --> 00:00:15.147
I knocked on the door,
and as I open the door,

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:17.515
the guy turns around and then,

00:00:17.515 --> 00:00:19.042
proceeds to throw up all over the girl

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:20.463
that he's having sex with.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.583
That happened.

00:00:21.593 --> 00:00:22.426
(swoosh)

00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:23.490
- I was actually closing the bar

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.160
at one of the places I
worked in Hell's Kitchen.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.720
Usually typical, when
you're closing the bar,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.630
wrapping everything down,
and then all of a sudden,

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.507
three guys walk in, and
one of the guys goes,

00:00:30.507 --> 00:00:31.920
"Hey, are you open?"

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.777
My manager and I were both like,

00:00:32.777 --> 00:00:35.100
"Oh, actually we're really
sorry but we are closed."

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.589
The registers are shut
down, like, everything.

00:00:36.589 --> 00:00:39.960
Our boss has started to mop
the floor, like, we were done.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.347
One of the guys turns
around to leave and he goes,

00:00:43.347 --> 00:00:44.520
"You don't know what you just did."

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.888
And we're like, wait, what?

00:00:45.888 --> 00:00:47.480
Like what, like what just happened?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.952
He was like, "That was Bruce
Willis you just closed on."

00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:51.009
And I was like,

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:52.518
(makes surprise sound).

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:53.366
- Was that really Bruce Willis?

00:00:53.366 --> 00:00:54.320
- It was really Bruce Willis.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.153
- Oh.

00:00:55.153 --> 00:00:56.220
- And so we actually felt really bad.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.130
The owner of the bar ended up

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.440
sending him a bottle of
tequila, a bottle of mezcal

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.510
just to say sorry.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.143
I feel terrible.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.481
- That would have been a great tip.

00:01:03.481 --> 00:01:04.403
- Right?

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.363
So yeah, I closed the
door on Bruce Willis.

00:01:07.473 --> 00:01:08.306
(swoosh)

00:01:08.306 --> 00:01:09.139
- So the other day, I actually had

00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:10.316
a group of four people come in.

00:01:10.316 --> 00:01:12.380
Right off the bat, the
one guy wanted to know

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.391
what our most expensive champagne was,

00:01:14.391 --> 00:01:17.120
which is not a question
that you get very often.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.550
I was like, well, Dom
Perignon like, $455 a bottle.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.646
And he just went, "Great, we'll take two."

00:01:22.646 --> 00:01:26.790
That's such a strange way
to just start balling out

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:27.623
on your evening.

00:01:27.623 --> 00:01:29.330
The people he was with were
like, "No, no, don't do it."

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:32.400
And he was like, "No, I'm Jay-Z
tonight, I'm balling out."

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.150
So I grabbed my manager 'cause I was like,

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.570
I think this is a little suspicious.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.460
And he was like, oh no,
if he ordered it, like,

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.640
let's do it, let's go.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.583
By the end of the couple
hours that they were there,

00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:44.658
the guy who had ordered
the champagne was like,

00:01:44.658 --> 00:01:47.143
laid back in his chair, just drinking

00:01:47.143 --> 00:01:48.733
straight out of the bottle.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:51.110
Absolutely hammered.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.070
You know that look on
someone's face, when like,

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.610
they can puke at any second.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.930
That's the world he's living in.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.557
He tried to walk out without paying.

00:01:57.557 --> 00:02:00.570
I grabbed my bouncer so fast.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.687
And he was just like, "Oh wait,
come on, (muffled sounds)."

00:02:02.687 --> 00:02:04.180
And I was like, Dude, I
have your credit card,

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.480
I'm gonna swipe it for this amount

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.379
and I'm gonna give myself 20% gratuity.

00:02:07.379 --> 00:02:10.270
We caught him real fast, and made him pay,

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.882
and I'm sure, even though
that was several days ago,

00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:14.381
he's still hungover.

00:02:14.381 --> 00:02:15.214
(swoosh)

00:02:15.214 --> 00:02:16.047
- I had this couple come in.

00:02:16.047 --> 00:02:17.590
They were so sweet, I guess
it was a regular date,

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:18.423
she looked really nice.

00:02:18.423 --> 00:02:20.840
The guy waited till she
got, kinda got buzzed,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.179
where she was like, semi-walking
straight in her heels.

00:02:23.179 --> 00:02:24.012
- Uh-oh.

00:02:24.012 --> 00:02:25.500
- She went to the bathroom, he's like,

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.090
Hide this ring in a red velvet cupcake

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.110
that we served at that place.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.300
So, we, all the bartenders are like,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.480
Oh my God, this guy's gonna propose,

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.480
we're about to be all snapped,

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.888
we're about to be on
camera, blah blah blah.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.721
- Yeah.

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.250
- We hide it in, we put the candle in.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.020
The guy gets down on one
knee, he's all excited,

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.330
you could tell he was like, nervous,

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.790
'cause all cameras in the
whole restaurant are on him.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:47.426
And the lady's like, "Hum,
can we talk about this first?"

00:02:47.426 --> 00:02:48.650
(surprise breathing)

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.547
I was like, uh-oh, because we can't move.

00:02:51.547 --> 00:02:52.406
- Oh my God.

00:02:52.406 --> 00:02:55.060
- Oh no, what do we do?

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.482
'Cause we still had to stay smiling.

00:02:56.482 --> 00:02:57.570
(laughs)

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.903
It was so awkward.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.010
- I'd be devastated.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.242
- He looked like he was gonna cry.

00:03:01.242 --> 00:03:02.588
- Oh, poor baby.

00:03:02.588 --> 00:03:04.671
(laughs)

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.183
- I guess the truth comes
out when you're drunk, right?

00:03:07.183 --> 00:03:09.083
- Girl, woo.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.440
- I was like, how can I handle

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.618
that situation without laughing?

00:03:11.618 --> 00:03:12.973
- Oh my God.
(laughs)

00:03:12.973 --> 00:03:15.560
- Without being like, I
wanted to be part of it

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.682
until it went into shambles.

00:03:16.682 --> 00:03:19.182
(jazzy music)

00:03:20.326 --> 00:03:21.731
(wind blowing)

00:03:21.731 --> 00:03:22.564
(metal squeaking)

